    <statement><p>For the following alternating series,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \sum_{n=1}^\infty a_n = 1 - \frac{1}{10} + \frac{1}{100} - \frac{1}{1000} + ...</m></p>
<p>how many terms do you have to go for your approximation (your partial sum) to be within 1e-07
from the convergent value of that series?</p>
<p><fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
